<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Deadbolt Network Stakeholder Report — {{ meta.run_id }}</title><style>:root{--ink:#17212b;--muted:#687582;--line:#dfe5e9;--brand:#087e9b;--bg:#edf1f3;--high:#c43c22}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);font:15px/1.55 Inter,system-ui,sans-serif}.page{max-width:960px;margin:28px auto;background:#fff;padding:48px 56px;box-shadow:0 2px 16px #17212b16}header{border-bottom:3px solid var(--brand);padding-bottom:24px}.eyebrow{color:var(--brand);font-size:11px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase}h1{font-size:29px;margin:5px 0}h2{font-size:19px;margin:34px 0 12px}.muted{color:var(--muted)}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:10px}.metric,.panel{padding:16px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:7px}.metric strong{font-size:25px;display:block}.notice{border-left:4px solid #d09a27;background:#fff8e8;padding:13px 16px}.finding{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:17px 0}.high{color:var(--high)}footer{border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:40px;padding-top:16px;color:var(--muted);font-size:12px}@media print{body{background:#fff}.page{box-shadow:none;margin:0;max-width:none}}</style></head><body><main class="page">
<header><div class="eyebrow">Deadbolt / Stakeholder brief</div><h1>Network Security Assessment</h1><div class="muted">{{ assessment_profile }} profile · {{ meta.run_id }} · {{ meta.finished_at[:10] }}</div></header>
<h2>Executive summary</h2><p>Deadbolt inventoried reachable hosts and services within the recorded authorization boundary. The assessment observed <strong>{{ summary.hosts_up }}</strong> reachable host{{ '' if summary.hosts_up == 1 else 's' }} and <strong>{{ summary.open_services }}</strong> open or potentially open service{{ '' if summary.open_services == 1 else 's' }}.</p>{% if findings %}<p class="high"><strong>{{ findings|length }} explicit automated vulnerability signal{{ '' if findings|length == 1 else 's' }} require analyst validation.</strong></p>{% else %}<p>No explicit automated vulnerability signals were reported. This does not establish that the environment is vulnerability-free.</p>{% endif %}
<h2>Assessment reach</h2><div class="grid">{% for item in coverage %}<div class="metric"><strong>{{ item.value }}</strong><span class="muted">{{ item.label }}</span></div>{% endfor %}<div class="metric"><strong>{{ quality.grade|upper }}</strong><span class="muted">Evidence quality</span></div></div>
<h2>Priority observations</h2>{% for item in findings %}<div class="finding"><strong class="{{ item.severity }}">{{ item.severity|upper }} · {{ item.title }}</strong><p>{{ item.metadata.description }}</p></div>{% else %}<p>No explicit vulnerability results were generated by the enabled scanner policy.</p>{% endfor %}{% if exposure_review %}<div class="panel"><strong>{{ exposure_review|length }} service exposure{{ '' if exposure_review|length == 1 else 's' }} queued for review</strong><p class="muted">Administrative, legacy, or cleartext services were observed. Their presence is not classified as a vulnerability until configuration and access controls are validated.</p></div>{% endif %}
<h2>Limitations and assurance</h2><div class="notice"><ul>{% for item in limitations %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></div>
<h2>Recommended next actions</h2><ol><li>Confirm that every observed service is expected, owned, and required.</li><li>Validate administrative and legacy services against segmentation and access-control requirements.</li><li>Reproduce explicit vulnerability signals before assigning remediation severity.</li><li>Perform credentialed configuration and patch assessment where authorization permits.</li><li>Retest after remediation and compare the normalized service inventory.</li></ol>
<footer>Concise stakeholder report. Host, port, service, OS, script, execution, and evidence details are available in <strong>technical-report.html</strong>.</footer></main></body></html>
